[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one bug and marked known, with one fix queued. The
reports say otherwise: they hold **three different problems**. One fix closes only the first.

<Callout>
Not one issue. Fixing the parser leaves the form hint and the one-day moves open.
</Callout>

## The three problems

<ProblemCounts ticket={4471} />

1. **Parser** ([issue #2](https://github.com/pablocabrera85/empty-repo/issues/2)). The shared parser reads every date month first. Day-first tenants get flipped dates. This is the bug #4471 describes.
2. **Form hint** ([issue #3](https://github.com/pablocabrera85/empty-repo/issues/3)). booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY`, so people at day-first tenants type month first. Only `form` reports at alder.physio, copper.studio and pale.harbour. The parser fix does not touch it.
3. **One-day move** ([issue #4](https://github.com/pablocabrera85/empty-repo/issues/4)). The desk already noted these in `desk-notes.json`, but they were still counted as parser. Looks like a time zone problem.

## What the data says

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

Intake tags are a guess from the reporter's browser. 15 of the 33 hint reports were tagged
`parser`, and 23 parser reports were tagged `hint`, so the tag cannot split a ticket.
Cause comes from the tenant's locale and booking form (`causeOf` in `src/lib/kb/causes.ts`).

The export also repeats 15 reports (427 rows, 412 unique), so counts here use one row per id.

## Why it was merged

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject alone. These reports share
subjects like "Wrong day on the invite" across three different causes. That decision's
consequences section only covers the opposite error, one bug under many subjects.

## Lessons

- A subject line cannot tell causes apart. Check the tenant's locale and form before merging.
- Count what a merged ticket covers, per cause, before marking it known.

